# ===========================================================
# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages
# ===========================================================
# IMPORTANT: this is intentionally ONE single rule for every path, not
# separate rules per section. Cloudflare Pages applies every matching
# _headers block simultaneously rather than letting a more specific path
# override a general one — so a "/*" block and an "/admin/*" block both
# fire for /admin/, and browsers enforce the strictest combination of
# both. That's what caused the CMS to load blank: the admin-friendly
# policy was always fighting the public-page policy. One combined policy
# below avoids that entirely.
#
# This means the policy is a bit looser overall than perfectly scoped
# per-section policies would be — it allows a few domains (unpkg.com,
# cdn.jsdelivr.net, unsafe-eval) on public pages that they don't
# actually use. That's an acceptable tradeoff for something that
# reliably works over something "tighter" that silently breaks the CMS
# or member portal.
# ===========================================================

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https: blob:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://script.google.com https://auth.decapbridge.com https://gateway.decapbridge.com https://api.github.com https://*.githubusercontent.com https://cykghfwuelikoqueqyoa.supabase.co https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
